list
[
  {
    "id": "P0001",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The existing tests pass, but the review found 21 issues: 4 High, 12 Medium and 5 Low. Fifteen behavioral issues were reproduced with local regression probes; the seeded-RNG finding rests on source inspection. Production files were left unchanged.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0002",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations below are relative to `/work/crate`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0003",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "High\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0004",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Disabling server configuration panics with pending connections\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0005",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/endpoint.rs:211`, `:540`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0006",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`set_server_config(None)` should allow the endpoint to stop accepting new connections without making ordinary processing panic. With an `Incoming` pending, receiving a retransmitted Initial panics at the configuration unwrap. Accepting that pending connection without an explicit override also panics.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0007",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `review_disable_server_with_pending_incoming` and `review_accept_pending_after_disable_server` both reproduced the panics. This can interrupt an application\u2019s shutdown or configuration-change flow.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0008",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "retain the configuration needed by pending incoming connections, or handle its absence explicitly.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0009",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "A rejected ordered read destroys the receive stream\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0010",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/connection/streams/recv.rs:269`, `:272`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0011",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "An ordered read after an unordered read should return `IllegalOrderedRead` while preserving the stream. Instead, `Chunks::new` removes the receive state before checking ordering; returning the error drops that state and any unread data.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0012",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `review_ordered_error_preserves_unordered_stream` read `abc` from `abcdef`, received the expected ordering error, then received `ClosedStream` when attempting to resume unordered reading. The corresponding control read successfully returned `def`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0013",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "validate ordering before removing the map entry, or restore the entry on failure.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0014",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Legal peer ACK-delay parameters can trigger a panic\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0015",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/connection/ack_frequency.rs:49`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0016",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "With ACK-frequency control enabled, the peer\u2019s minimum delay must remain usable even when it exceeds the RTT-based preferred upper bound. The code instead calls `clamp` with inverted bounds.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0017",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `review_peer_min_ack_delay_above_rtt_is_supported` successfully decoded parameters specifying a 100 ms minimum and maximum ACK delay, then reproduced `assertion failed: min <= max` with a 10 ms RTT. The helper is called when constructing ACK-frequency requests.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0018",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "make the upper bound at least the peer\u2019s minimum delay.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0019",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Optional transport-parameter integers panic instead of returning an error\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0020",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/transport_parameters.rs:472`, `:479`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0021",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Malformed parameter values should produce the existing decoding error. These branches instead unwrap a failed integer decode.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0022",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: the public-API probe decoded `20 00`\u2014a DATAGRAM-size parameter with an empty value\u2014and panicked with `UnexpectedEnd`. An empty minimum-ACK-delay value reproduced the same failure in the other branch.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0023",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Consequently, callers cannot handle these ordinary decoder errors through `Result`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0024",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "decode within the declared parameter length, propagate errors with `?`, and verify complete value consumption.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0025",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Medium\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0026",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Stop followed by reset returns receive credit twice\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0027",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/connection/streams/state.rs:356`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0028",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Stopping a receive stream already credits its discarded unread bytes. A subsequent reset credits those bytes again because it subtracts `bytes_read` rather than accounting for the earlier stop.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0029",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: with a 100-byte receive window, `review_stop_then_reset_returns_credit_once` received and stopped 50 bytes, processed the peer\u2019s reset, then allowed 150 additional unread bytes. The final write returned `Ok(50)` instead of `Blocked`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0030",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "This exceeds the receiver\u2019s configured buffering budget. Existing `stopped_reset` coverage checks cleanup but not this accounting.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0031",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "for stopped streams, credit only any increase beyond the previously accounted end offset.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0032",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Restoring a receive window grants additional unintended credit\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0033",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/connection/streams/state.rs:874`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0034",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Increasing a previously reduced window should first cancel outstanding shrink debt. Instead, the implementation immediately increases `local_max_data` while retaining that debt.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0035",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `review_receive_window_restore_does_not_expand_credit` changed the window from 100 to 50 and back to 100 without reading data. The sender could then write 150 bytes. The unchanged-window control allowed 100.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0036",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "consume shrink debt before granting additional advertised credit.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0037",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Zero MTU minimum change prevents discovery from finishing\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0038",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/connection/mtud.rs:333`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0039",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`minimum_change(0)` is accepted without a documented restriction. It makes the stopping comparison permanently false, so the search repeatedly probes an unchanged size.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0040",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `review_zero_mtu_minimum_change_eventually_finishes`, using a 10 ms RTT, exhausted 100 simulation steps after sending 49 successful probes with no losses. Discovery remained at 1451 bytes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0041",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Applications selecting this boundary value incur continuing unnecessary traffic and wakeups.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0042",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "reject or clamp zero, or terminate explicitly when the search cannot advance.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0043",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Failed connection attempts retain allocated CID routing state\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0044",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/endpoint.rs:344`, `:355`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0045",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "A connection attempt that returns an error should release its provisional state. `new_cid` inserts routing state before the fallible crypto-session creation, and the error path does not remove it.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0046",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `review_failed_connect_releases_cid` used an invalid server name. `connect` returned `InvalidServerName` and reported zero open connections, but retained one known CID.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0047",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Repeated failed attempts therefore retain memory and consume CID capacity.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0048",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "roll back the provisional CID on error, or defer committing routing state until session creation succeeds.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0049",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Valid longer integer encodings are rejected\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0050",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/transport_parameters.rs:487`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0051",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "QUIC variable-length integers may use a longer permitted encoding. The decoder compares the declared length with the decoded value\u2019s *minimum* encoding size, incorrectly requiring canonical encoding.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0052",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: the public probe supplied `04 02 40 01`, representing `initial_max_data = 1` using two bytes. It returned `Err(Malformed)`. A control confirmed that the primitive integer decoder accepts `40 01`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0053",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "This can reject otherwise valid peer transport parameters.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0054",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "compare the declared length with bytes actually consumed, rather than `value.size()`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0055",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Datagram eviction ignores the incoming datagram\u2019s size\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0056",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/connection/datagrams.rs:39`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0057",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The documented send-buffer limit should cause older queued datagrams to be evicted when necessary. The eviction condition checks only the bytes already queued.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0058",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: with a four-byte buffer, `review_datagram_drop_respects_buffer_limit` queued `aaaa` and `bbbb` with dropping enabled. Both were delivered; the expected retained queue contained only `bbbb`. The control correctly blocked the second send when dropping was disabled.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0059",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "account for the incoming length during eviction, and define handling for a single datagram larger than the buffer.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0060",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "TLS configuration conversion succeeds before session creation panics\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0061",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/crypto/rustls.rs:384`, `:366`, `:515`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0062",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The documentation says TLS 1.3 must be enabled for conversion to succeed. Conversion checks the provider\u2019s initial cipher suite but does not validate the enabled protocol versions.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0063",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: with `rustls/tls12` enabled, a TLS-1.2-only client configuration converted successfully. Calling `connect` then panicked on `General(\"TLS 1.3 support is required for QUIC\")`. A server configuration with `max_early_data_size = 1024` likewise converted and later panicked during acceptance.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0064",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Callers receive delayed panics after a successful fallible conversion.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0065",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "validate QUIC compatibility during conversion and preserve recoverable session-creation errors.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0066",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Qlog RTT values use seconds instead of milliseconds\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0067",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/connection/paths.rs:267`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0068",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Qlog RTT metrics require milliseconds. All four RTT-related fields are populated using `as_secs_f32()`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0069",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `review_qlog_rtt_uses_milliseconds` supplied 100 ms and observed `Some(0.1)` instead of `Some(100.0)`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0070",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "This makes latency measurements in exported traces 1,000 times too small.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0071",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "convert these durations to fractional milliseconds.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0072",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "CID validation panics on short connection IDs\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0073",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/cid_generator.rs:147`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0074",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`validate` should return `InvalidCid` for an ID that could not have been generated. Its unconditional `split_at(3)` instead panics for shorter IDs.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0075",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: public-API calls reproduced panics for CID lengths 0, 1 and 2. Longer tested lengths returned validation results.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0076",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Applications using this public validator must currently add an undocumented length check.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0077",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "reject an incorrect total length before splitting.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0078",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Safe stream-ID construction can violate the VarInt invariant\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0079",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/lib.rs:257`, `:280`, `:301`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0080",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`StreamId::new` accepts an unrestricted `u64` index, although only 60 bits fit. Conversion then bypasses the documented VarInt range requirement.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0081",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: the public probe constructed a client unidirectional stream with index `1 << 60`. Converting it produced `4611686018427387906`, exceeding `VarInt::MAX`. Source inspection shows encoding subsequently unwraps a failed checked conversion.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0082",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "validate the index and provide a checked construction path; constrain every generation path to the representable range.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0083",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "An explicit RNG seed still invokes the OS entropy source\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0084",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/endpoint.rs:77`; contract at `quinn-proto/src/config/mod.rs:154`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0085",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The seed option is documented as supporting environments without an entropy source. However, `map_or` eagerly evaluates `StdRng::from_os_rng()` even when the seed is present.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0086",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: source inspection establishes the unconditional entropy call; the dependency documents that this call panics when entropy acquisition fails. An entropy failure was not injected locally.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0087",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "use lazy default evaluation, such as `map_or_else`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0088",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Default-feature documentation fails\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0089",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/crypto/rustls.rs:279`, `quinn-proto/src/connection/qlog.rs:45`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0090",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Documentation should build under the default feature configuration. Unconditional links reference items that are compiled out.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0091",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: strict public rustdoc failed on `with_platform_verifier`; adding private-item documentation also exposed the missing `QlogStream` link. Documentation passed with both relevant features enabled.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0092",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "conditionally document these links, or use references that remain valid when the features are disabled.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0093",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Low\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0094",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Datagram size reporting contradicts local disablement\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0095",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/connection/datagrams.rs:69`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0096",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`max_size()` documents `None` when datagrams are disabled locally, but does not check local configuration.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0097",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: `review_datagram_max_size_disabled_locally` observed `Some(1414)` after local disablement, although `send` returns `Disabled`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0098",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "apply the same local-enable check in both methods.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0099",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Stream-accessor panic preconditions are undocumented\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0100",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/connection/mod.rs:421`, `:432`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0101",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The public documentation only says these methods provide stream control. Source inspection shows that requesting the wrong half of a unidirectional stream immediately asserts, before a caller can receive a `ClosedStream` error.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0102",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "document the direction requirements and panics, or expose a fallible accessor.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0103",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The advisory pass flagged 37 missing `# Errors` sections and 11 missing `# Panics` sections. These two accessors have concrete undocumented caller preconditions; invariant-only panic warnings were not treated as additional defects.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0104",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Public types lack useful diagnostic implementations\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0105",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/token.rs:67`, `quinn-proto/src/connection/paths.rs:285`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0106",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The default-feature advisory pass identified 21 reachable public types without `Debug`, excluding three inaccessible range-set implementation types.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0107",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "VarInt conversion narrows u128 before validating its range. quinn-proto/src/varint.rs:106. The TryFrom<u128> implementation narrows the input to u64 before applying the 62-bit VarInt bound, so high bits are discarded before validation. For example, VarInt::try_from((1u128 << 64) + 7) succeeds as VarInt(7), although the public conversion contract requires an error for every value at or above 2^62. Callers converting wide application counters can therefore serialize a different integer without receiving VarIntBoundsExceeded.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0108",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "A concrete consequence is that `Result<(), TokenReuseError>` cannot be used with ordinary `unwrap` or `expect`; the missing implementations also hinder diagnostics.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0109",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "derive `Debug` where appropriate and provide selective manual implementations for stateful types.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0110",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Unchecked conversions lack invariant explanations\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0111",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/connection/send_buffer.rs:99`, `:118`; `quinn-proto/src/connection/mod.rs:3261`; `quinn-proto/src/lib.rs:280`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0112",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Four unchecked VarInt conversions lack SAFETY comments explaining why their values fit. This obscures the bounds future changes must preserve; finding 14 demonstrates that one assumed bound already fails.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0113",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Evidence: advisory lint output and source inspection.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0114",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "establish the bounds first, then document them beside each unchecked conversion.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0115",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Strict Clippy fails on the supplied toolchain\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0116",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "`quinn-proto/src/connection/assembler.rs:333`, `quinn-proto/src/connection/packet_crypto.rs:91`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0117",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Both default and expanded-feature Clippy runs failed under Rust 1.99.1 because `-D warnings` promotes `derivable_impls` and `manual_filter` diagnostics to errors.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0118",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "derive the enum default and use `Option::filter`. These failures predate the review edits; comparison against an older compiler was unavailable.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0119",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Verification\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0120",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Host: aarch64 Linux, Rust 1.99.1, Clippy 0.1.99, rustfmt 1.10.0. Checks used installed tools and prefetched dependencies; no tools or dependencies were installed.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0121",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Executed from `/work/crate`:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0122",
    "report": "A",
